# Derived joint and observational kernels of a generalized SCM

Given a gSCM `M`, the joint kernel `jointKernel M : Kernel (FixedValues M) (RandomValues M)`
is the pushforward of the latent product measure `M.latentProduct` along the evaluation
map `M.evalMap` (see `Causal/Model/Evaluation.lean`), with the fixed-value argument `s`
threaded as the kernel parameter.  The observational kernel `obsKernel M` is then the
pushforward of `jointKernel M` onto the observed coordinates `V ⊆ V ∪ L`.

The construction uses `Kernel.compProd` of the constant kernel at `M.latentProduct`
and the deterministic kernel of `Function.uncurry M.evalMap`, followed by a
`Kernel.map Prod.snd`.  `obsCondKernel` is the jointly measurable
kernel-native conditional object built via Mathlib's `Kernel.condKernel`.

Do-calculus Rule 2 / Rule 3 kernel-level theorems (and their value-space
plumbing) have been factored out to:
  * `Causalean/Causal/Do/Rule2.lean` — Rule 2 + `fillZrW` helpers.
  * `Causalean/Causal/Do/Rule3.lean` — Rule 3 + compat bridge lemmas.

## References

* Basic Concepts.tex, Definition `def:scm-joint` (joint and observational kernels).':
