⚠ [3463/3564] Replayed Causalean.Estimation.NPIV.Operator
warning: Causalean/Estimation/NPIV/Operator.lean:4:0: * 'Authors: Jiyuan Tan

# Concrete projection operator for the TRAE rate theorem

This file defines the concrete projection operator
    `T h := Π_{Q̄} ∘ E[· | σ(Z)]`
used in the simplified rate theorem of
`doc/basic_concepts/po/estimation/trae_inverse_problems.tex` (lines 250–384).

## Design

`Setup.lean` keeps `Hbar`, `Qbar` as plain function sets without
Hilbert structure, since the mixed-bias proof only needs algebraic linearity.
The rate theorem requires an L² realization: closed subspaces
`Hbar_L2`, `Qbar_L2 : Submodule ℝ (Lp ℝ 2 μ)` of the *ambient* `Lp ℝ 2 μ`,together with embeddings of function-level members.  We choose the ambient
`Lp ℝ 2 μ` (rather than pushforward `Lp ℝ 2 (μ.map X)`) so the conditional
expectation `condExpL2` can be applied directly without pushforward
identifications.

The σ-algebra "generated by `Z`" is encoded as
`m_Z := MeasurableSpace.comap S.zOf S.inst𝒵 ∘ (... lifted along W)` —
concretely `MeasurableSpace.comap (zOf ∘ W) inst𝒵`, with a hypothesis
`m_Z_le : m_Z ≤ m₀`.

The operator `T h` is then:
1.  lift `h ∘ X : Ω → ℝ` into `Lp ℝ 2 μ` (via a `MemLp` hypothesis on
    `OperatorSystem`);
2.  apply `MeasureTheory.condExpL2 ℝ ℝ m_Z_le` (a continuous linear map into
    the σ(Z)-measurable subspace);
3.  project onto `Qbar_L2` via `Submodule.orthogonalProjectionFn`.

The single population identity exported here, `T_inner_eq_integral`, is what
the rate theorem consumes.  Its proof combines `condExpL2` self-adjointness
with the orthogonality characterization of `Qbar_L2`-projection; it is fully
proved (no sorries).

The adjoint `T*` and the self-adjoint composite `T†T` are bundled in
`Operator/Adjoint.lean`; this file focuses on the unbundled projection operator
and the population identity needed by the DR rate argument.':
