warning: Causalean/Graph/CComponents.lean:4:0: * 'Authors: Jiyuan Tan

# C-Components (Confounded Components)

This file defines C-components for SWIG Graphs.
Two observed variables are "directly confounded" if they share an unobserved parent.
C-components are the connected components of the bidirected projection graph.

## Main definitions

* `SWIGGraph.directlyConfounded` — two observed variables share an unobserved parent
* `SWIGGraph.bidirectedReachable` — transitive closure of directly-confounded relation
* `SWIGGraph.cComponents` — the C-component decomposition (as an `Array`)
* `SWIGGraph.cComponentSet` — the C-components as a canonical `Finset (Finset _)`
  (`observed.image cComponentOf`), the order-independent index used by the
  c-component factorization

## Main results

* `bidirectedReachable_{symm,trans}` (+ `_head`, `_observed_left/right`) — bidirected
  reachability is an equivalence relation on the observed nodes.
* `mem_bidirectedBFS_iff_reachable` — the BFS `cComponentOf` computes exactly the
  bidirected-reachable set (correctness of the fuel-bounded search).
* `cComponentSet_biUnion` — the c-components cover the observed nodes.
* `cComponentSet_pairwise_disjoint` — distinct c-components are disjoint.
  Together these state that `cComponentSet` **partitions** `observed`.

## References

* Basic Concepts.tex, Definition 5 (C-component)':
