# Indicator spans and partition-cell statistics over a weighted support

For a `WeightedSupport R` (see `Causalean/Panel/Weighted/Support.lean`) and a
classifier `G : R → 𝒢` (or two classifiers `G, T` on parallel axes), we
build:

* the **one-axis indicator span** `indicatorSpan G : Submodule ℝ (R → ℝ)`
  generated by the singleton indicators `r ↦ if G r = g then 1 else 0`, one per value `g : 𝒢`;
* the **two-axis indicator span** `twoAxisIndicatorSpan G T` generated by
  the union of the per-axis singleton indicators on the two classifiers;
* partition-cell statistics `cellMass G g` and positive-mass cell means
  `cellMean F G g hpos` on a `WeightedSupport R`.

This is the finite, non-measure-theoretic counterpart of the cell-bridge
constructions used elsewhere in the panel library. It is intended for weighted
finite supports where sums over observed records are the primitive operation.':
