warning: Causalean/Panel/EstimandCharacterization/OLSWeightDecomposition/GeneralCondExp.lean:4:0: * 'Authors: Jiyuan Tan

# Słoczyński (2022): general (continuous-covariate) overlap-weighted ATE

Abstract-conditioning version of the saturated-control OLS theorem
`thm:po-estimand-sloczynski-ols-overlap-weighted-ate` for an *arbitrary*
covariate σ-algebra `m` (think: `m` generated by a covariate `X`). This uses
Mathlib's σ-algebra conditional expectation `μ[f | m]` rather than the
finite-event `eventCondExp` used elsewhere in this repo, so it covers the
continuous-`X` case directly.

## Setup

`D : Ω → ℝ` is binary treatment (`D = 0 ∨ D = 1` a.e.), `Y0 Y1` are the
square-integrable potential outcomes, `Y` the observed outcome. Write
`p := μ[D | m]` (propensity score) and `D̃ := D − p` (the saturated residual
of `D` on the controls). The saturated-control OLS estimand is the
Frisch–Waugh–Lovell ratio

    β_sat = E[D̃·Y] / E[D̃²].

The theorem `saturated_ols_overlap_weighted_ate` proves the totalized
ratio identity

    β_sat = E[p(1−p)·(μ[Y1 | m] − μ[Y0 | m])] / E[p(1−p)].

The equality also covers zero integrated overlap because both ratios use Lean's
totalized division convention.

## Conditional-mean-independence faithfulness note

The hypotheses `hCMI1`, `hCMI0` are stated in the **mean-independence
factoring form**

    μ[D·Y1 | m] =ᵐ μ[D | m]·μ[Y1 | m],   μ[(1−D)·Y0 | m] =ᵐ μ[1−D | m]·μ[Y0 | m].

This is a *consequence* of the paper's full conditional mean independence
`E[Y(d) | D, X] = E[Y(d) | X]` (derive it by the tower property: condition
on the joint σ-algebra `m ⊔ comap D`, factor out the `m ⊔ comap D`-measurable
`D` / `1−D`, then apply CMI to replace `μ[Y(d)|m ⊔ comap D]` by `μ[Y(d)|m]`).
Taking the factored form as a hypothesis is therefore a *weakening* of the
paper's assumption, not a strengthening — the resulting theorem is more
general, not less faithful.':
